//    so that this remains true even if we later change the memory layout.
//  - For each fixed i, we restrict the 'j' traversal to [0, i),
//    eliminating the inner-loop conditional `if (j < i)` and avoiding
//    useless iterations.
//  - We accumulate into a scalar `accum` instead of repeatedly updating
//    x[i] in memory. This makes the inner loop a simple reduction over j,
//    which compilers handle efficiently (and is friendlier to vectorization).
